From: abhay-byte <zenithblue.dev@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 04:30:52 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] panvk: transcode BC1-BC5 to ETC2/EAC shadows and drop
 unreadable raw planes

Recreates the lost RC4-lowmem BC patch (see
worklogs/g615-dxvk/rc4-binary-analysis.md, "Result 3") on top of the
150/151/180/185 fragment-decode shadows, with its readback bug fixed.

Gate (panvk_bc_lowmem_enabled()): v10+ (CSF), BC emulation on, the
fragment decode path available (no PANVK_DEBUG=bc_compute/no_gs) and all
ten ETC2/EAC formats native. On by default like the released RC4-lowmem
binary; PANVK_BC_MODE=exact keeps the exact shadows (unknown values also
fall back to exact, with a warning). The log line becomes
"panvk: BC emulation on, lowmem (native compressed mask ...)".

Per image (2D bc_gfx images only; OPTIMAL tiling; no SPARSE_*, DISJOINT,
ALIAS, BLOCK_TEXEL_VIEW_COMPATIBLE, external memory or HOST_TRANSFER
usage; BC4/BC5 with MUTABLE_FORMAT only with a format list of their own
format, since the EAC shadow fixes the signedness):

  bc_lowmem = 1, BC1-BC5: bc_shadow is an ETC2/EAC image, U-interleaved,
    SAMPLED only, sRGB from the view:
      BC1 RGB  -> ETC2 RGB8         BC1 RGBA -> ETC2 RGB8A1
      BC2/BC3  -> ETC2 RGBA8        BC4      -> EAC R11 (signed)
      BC5      -> EAC RG11 (signed)
  bc_lowmem = 2, BC6H/BC7 without a raw plane: the exact shadow.
  bc_no_raw: no TRANSFER_SRC usage, so the raw blocks can never be read
    back. planes[0] gets no memory and is never written.

The transcoder (bc/panvk_bc_etc2.comp, SPIR-V header built by gen_spv.sh,
run through vk_meta like the 022/150 decoders) runs one invocation per
block: exact BC decode, then ETC1 differential/individual (both flips),
ETC2 H and planar modes for colour and a 16-table EAC search for
alpha/R11/RG11, written straight into the U-interleaved shadow plane.
The encoder is written in the common GLSL/C subset; a host test that
includes it and decodes with Mesa's texcompress_etc.c finds bit-exact
agreement on 20000 random blocks for every mode, and on a synthetic
picture (crude BC encoder) PSNR against the exact BC decode of
BC1/BC3 colour 38.7 dB, BC3 alpha 49.1 dB, BC4 49.3 dB.

PANVK_BC_LM_OPTS is kept, with new bit meanings (default 0x30000):
0x10000 try the planar mode, 0x20000 try the H mode (both off: 34.6 dB on
BC1), 0x40000 EAC base codeword +-1 search (+0.5 dB, 3x the EAC work).
No device BO: zero-initialized raw-less images transcode a zeroed block
row from command buffer memory, read with zero pitches.

Readback bug fix. RC4-lowmem never stored the raw blocks, so
vkCmdCopyImage from BC images, image->buffer readback and host copies
were wrong for all 16 formats. Raw blocks can only be read back from
TRANSFER_SRC (or HOST_TRANSFER) images, so those keep the raw plane and
every readback and BC-source copy is bit-exact, as on the exact path;
they still get the ETC2/EAC shadow (BC1-BC5: raw + shadow = 2x the BC
size, about -33% against 180/185). Images without TRANSFER_SRC drop the
raw plane (RC4-lowmem sizes). Copies into those transcode or decode from
the source's raw plane (a copy source always has TRANSFER_SRC), or for a
non-BC source from a staging copy in command buffer memory. Trade-off:
DXVK sets TRANSFER_SRC on every texture, so under DXVK the saving is the
shadow part only. Transcoding copies from the decoded data (option b)
would give DXVK the full saving, but raw readback would still need a BC
re-encoder, so it does not fix the bug.

Tested GPU: none yet (host bitstream test only, see
 worklogs/bc-emul-perf/lowmem-197.md for the device test plan)
Mesa base range: 5a07217f034b3e50d8c7c7794f97a2df1742613b
Dependencies: csf-v11/022, 040, 108, 150, 151, 180, 185
Validation test: device plan in worklogs/bc-emul-perf/lowmem-197.md
 (bc_decode/bc_verify 16/16 with PANVK_BC_MODE=exact and raw readback
 exact by default, vkCmdCopyImage BC test for all 16 formats, PSNR vs
 exact, bc_perf memory)

